bluejay (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First packaged build of Bluejay, a native markdown note app: a file tree,
    a plain text editor and a live preview side by side, drawn by
    eframe/egui rather than by a web engine.

  * The window is a backdrop with the editor and the preview on it as rounded
    cards, standing off every edge and off one another. The tree keeps its
    place on the backdrop, and the status line runs the width of the window
    under both cards so that they end together.

  * Nothing is drawn along a pane's edge while it is being dragged, and the
    tree, the editor and the preview each have a floor they cannot be dragged
    past.

  * Two arrows at the top of the sidebar walk back and forward through the
    notes this window has shown.

  * The picker can make the folder it is looking for, and the first-run screen
    sits in the middle of the window rather than along its left edge.

 -- caganerg <caganergun@tutanota.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:10:06 +0300
